---
layout: base.njk
title: ConductVR
project: "conductvr"
instrument: true
---
{% from "github.njk" import githubButton %}

<div class="w-full">
  <img src="/images/pic26.jpg" alt="ConductVR Banner" class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl mb-12">
  
  <div class="text-center mb-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl tracking-tight uppercase font-bold text-white" style="letter-spacing: 0.1em;">ConductVR</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-gray-400">An educational tool for learning conducting in Virtual Reality</p>
  </div>
  
  <div class="flex justify-center mb-16">{{ githubButton("https://github.com/tgraves719/the-virtual-baton") }}</div>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 uppercase tracking-wide">The Challenge</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Learning the precise patterns for conducting is a foundational skill for any music student or ensemble leader. Traditionally, this is taught using 2D diagrams in textbooks, which can be difficult to translate into fluid, three-dimensional motion.</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mt-8 mb-4 uppercase tracking-wide">The Solution</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-400">ConductVR provides an immersive practice room where students can learn and master these patterns. With clear visual guides and a simple interface, the application makes the abstract tangible, allowing users to trace patterns in 3D space with their own hands.</p>
    </div>
    <img src="/images/pic07.jpg" alt="Diagram of a 4/4 conducting pattern" class="rounded-xl shadow-lg">
  </div>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center mt-24">
    <img src="/images/pic08.jpg" alt="The user interface for selecting conducting patterns in ConductVR" class="rounded-xl shadow-lg order-2 md:order-1">
    <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 uppercase tracking-wide">Features</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-gray-400 space-y-2">
        <li>Intuitive menu for selecting common time signatures (2/4, 3/4, 4/4, 6/8, etc.).</li>
        <li>Visualizations for both left and right-hand patterns.</li>
        <li>"Conducting Cube" mode for practicing within a defined space.</li>
        <li>Baton visualization for a more realistic practice experience.</li>
        <li>Built in Unity, leveraging its powerful VR development capabilities.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#
    ConductAR: ConductVR's premise moved off the headset and onto a webcam or phone.
    The app is vendored in instruments/conductar/ (tools/vendor-conductar.mjs) and
    runs entirely in the browser: camera frames are tracked on the device and never
    sent anywhere. The frame asks for the camera only when "Start camera" is pressed.
  #}
  <section id="conductar" class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mt-28 scroll-mt-28">
    <img src="/images/conductar-banner.jpg" alt="ConductAR" class="w-full h-auto rounded-xl mb-8">
    <p class="text-center text-lg text-gray-300 mb-8">Conduct along with a recording and see what your hands are actually doing.</p>
    <iframe src="/instruments/conductar/" title="ConductAR" loading="lazy"
            allow="camera; microphone; autoplay; fullscreen" allowfullscreen
            class="block w-full rounded-xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-black" style="height: max(640px, 85vh);"></iframe>
    <p class="mt-4 text-center text-sm"><a href="/instruments/conductar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-white uppercase tracking-wider">Full screen</a></p>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-16 mb-8">
    <a href="/work/" class="interactive-rainbow inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-md font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">&larr; Back</a>
  </div>
</div>